														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4617689">
									

<p>There are quite a few spelling and grammar errors that need correcting:<br />
*During the second log there's a bit which goes: 'The gestures it's tail'.<br />
*In SCP-5770 Events - 16.2.21 the word &quot;we're&quot; is used where 'were' should be used.<br />
*In SCP-5770 Events - 17.2.21, I don't really understand the meaning behind 'engage with an alligator'. What does 'engage' mean here?<br />
*'the bodies of which have been covered by brown sheet'.<br />
*'Dr. Pasqua is staging in front' should probably be 'standing'<br />
*'cricified'<br />
*'d-class' where it should probably be D-class or D-Class.</p>
<p>I think there are other times where the tone and style of writing can definitely be improved. For instance this sentence:</p>
<p>'How in the hell did they manage this and of course I didn't have the camera set up but it would have been pointless'</p>
<p>It could really do with being broken up with some punctuation. There are times when punctuation should be used, but isn't. Sometimes the tone of the article doesn't sound appropriate to a Foundation report, in my personal opinion. It's hard to lay my finger on exactly. Also, in the logs I feel there's sometimes an inconsistency where sometimes past tense is used (e.g. 'raised') and other times it isn't (e.g. 'walks'). It's definitely not a bad article though, I just think it needs cleaning up a bit.</p>

							</div>

								
					
